    rdfs:label "Evidence for Cassia Buds used in Chocolate & Confectionery: P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 86"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "CASSIA-BUDS: the immature flowers (perianth and ovary), gathered and dried, of several species of cinnamon, chiefly used in confectionery, having the flavour and pungency of cassia."@en ;
